# 13. HANDLE ASSIGNMENTS, ACTIVITIES, TESTS AND EXAMINATIONS DIFFERENTLY

The existing assessment system supports different work types:

- ASSIGNMENT
- ACTIVITY
- TEST
- EXAMINATION

Their time and exit behaviour should not be treated identically.

## A. Assignments and Activities

These should support a save-and-exit or pause-and-resume workflow.

Where a timed Assignment or Activity is configured:

- Provide an explicit Pause / Save and Exit action.
- Persist the pause state.
- Persist the remaining time or equivalent server-authoritative timing information.
- Allow the student to resume later.
- Resume from the correct remaining time.

For untimed work, simply save progress and allow the student to leave and return.

Do not lose previously entered answers.

## B. Tests and Examinations

Tests and Examinations must not have a pause feature.

Their timers must continue counting even when the student:

- Leaves the assessment page.
- Reloads the browser.
- Navigates away.
- Closes and reopens the assessment.

The deadline must remain authoritative.

When the student returns, calculate the actual remaining time from the existing attempt deadline.

When the deadline expires, run the normal expiry and submission process.

A test or examination must never receive extra time because the student navigated away.

## C. Important implementation safeguards

Do not accidentally introduce a universal pause mechanism that also pauses tests and examinations.

Do not reset timers when a component mounts again.

Use persisted server-side state and appropriate transactional operations for pausing or resuming Assignment and Activity attempts.

Ensure pause and resume cannot be abused to create extra examination time.

Preserve all existing submission and deadline protections.

